hello and welcome to inside the Oscars  I'm Rachel Smith in today's best picture  close-up discover how director Martin  Scorsese and actors Leonardo DiCaprio  and Jonah Hill went wild to tell the  saga of the wolf of Wall Street when I  was reading the book I thought this  can't possibly be true if it is true  first of all I didn't I couldn't believe  the guy who wrote it was gonna be alive  at the end of it and if it is true it's  wildly embellished and I spoke to the  FBI agent who arrested Jordan and he  said I will tell you this I tracked this  guy for 10 years every single thing in  this book is true every outlandish  coincidence every insane level of drug  taking the money everything is there  it's all true I didn't respond right  away to the material I couldn't find a  way in yet on it because of similarity  of the work that have done before in  other pictures and so if we're gonna do  that I thought well I'm gonna have to  really find a way to break a structure  somehow or evolve a style finally I said  all right I think I got the idea of how  to tell the story to ignore the  conventionality of certain story aspects  in fact just drop them so I had two that  we were in our script meetings and I  would anything that I found that I'd  seen before as let's lose it I started  to fight the continuity of it I said  what if it's just inside the mindset of  this world  what if it's inside the mindset of the  people want to take advantage of you and  me and want to beat you out of your  money and laugh at you when they do you  know they may change later on in life  and everything meantime you're hurt but  why don't we just stay with them wait  and then suddenly you turn around and  realize we would with in a sense with  monsters I was just taken by  you know Jordan's honesty and look he  looks at this as a very isolated time in  his life so he was incredibly forthright  with all this information not only in  the novel but for me as an actor  incredibly embarrassing details about  his life and to be able to go in there  with the idea that we're not gonna do  something conventional and every time we  tried you know our our characters  steered to some sort of you know  artificial sentimentality or some  motivation for his actions we would chop  it off at the head and then you know  bring him right back down to you know  who he is on a very authentic level and  the way Jordan betrayed himself in the  book it's a very hedonistic amoral time  period in his life so you know every  time we started going in that direction  all of us would you know say no you know  we've seen this before we seen so forth  I love three things I love my country I  love Jesus Christ and I love making  people rich this is a guy with no  impulse control you know I recognize who  this guy is and I really wanted the  chance to bring him to life and these  guys cared a lot more about becoming  excessively wealthy than what they had  to do to get there or who they had to  hurt to get there you don't see the wake  of destruction the ship just keeps  moving forward these guys just keep  going constantly forward without any  regard for anyone except themselves  that's the that's what we're we're  trying to capture in that culture you  know I mean something about the darker  nature of all of us to make sure you  don't miss any of the behind the scenes  action on Oscar Sunday  check out the Oscar buzz page on Oscar  com
 

